00:02:47.961 --> 00:02:48.460
Thank you.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.470
All right.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:53.970
What if we're able to maximize
the ad revenue that retailers

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:57.857
have through real-time
shopper analytics

00:02:57.857 --> 00:02:59.940
to see how their shoppers
are actually interacting

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.450
with the products and within
the store-- their traffic

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.450
and all of that.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:12.390
So our goal is to revolutionize
video and IoT intelligence

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:18.150
and bring that together, from
this era of unstructured data--

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.090
very forensic-- and
after-the-fact type

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:26.490
of thing to more of a structured
and preventative and a way

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:29.950
to be able to react on the spot.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.950
Let me explain a little bit
more about what the unstructured

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.440
versus structured data is.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.190
So unstructured data is
very blobby and homogeneous,

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.990
just like water flowing.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.380
It's just going
through, into the cloud.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.340
You can't really do
anything with it,

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.110
unless you have some
sort of human element,

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.340
human interaction with
it to tell you what it

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.900
is that's actually happening.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.750
Now, there are ways to be
able to detect disturbances

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.230
in that field, such
as motion detection.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.130
But it still doesn't
give you enough.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.370
You still need a human
there to tell you, oh, that

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:05.050
was just a bug--

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.750
literally, a bug
flying on the camera.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.360
Or it was a blurry
camera screen.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.190
Or it was actually a
human doing something.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:12.970
Right?

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.800
And, again, it's reactive.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.899
It happens after the fact.

00:04:17.899 --> 00:04:21.320
So with the advent of AI
and bringing everything up

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.610
into the cloud, we're
able to add more structure

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.230
to that data, be
able to tell you

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.459
what is actually in the
video that you are seeing.

00:04:29.459 --> 00:04:31.500
Such as in this scenario,
we're able to see there

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.312
are six people running.

00:04:33.312 --> 00:04:34.270
You know, that's great.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.769
We're able to know that there
are actually six people there.

00:04:36.769 --> 00:04:38.306
We know it's not
a blurry screen.

00:04:38.306 --> 00:04:40.180
We know there's no smudge
there or something.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.555
But we know there
are six people.

00:04:41.555 --> 00:04:42.700
However, they're running.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.575
Why are they running?

00:04:43.575 --> 00:04:44.680
We don't know exactly why.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.720
We still don't
have enough context

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.760
to be able to react
to that, right?

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.660
So we need a little bit more.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.540
That's where IoT
comes in and being

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.054
able to correlate all
of that data together.

00:04:55.054 --> 00:04:56.470
So in this particular
scenario, we

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.500
know that six people running.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.000
We know they weren't exercising
because it seemed like there

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.240
was a big spike in temperature.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:03.760
All right.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.860
We don't know what that spike
in temperature was because of.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:06.651
It could be a fire.

00:05:06.651 --> 00:05:08.470
More than likely, it's a fire.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:12.930
But we're going to be proactive
and go sound the alarm so we

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.550
get more and more people
out of the building

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.465
to save lives and
things like that.

00:05:17.465 --> 00:05:19.090
And then, after the
fact, we can always

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.360
figure out, forensics-wise,
who, what, where, why, and when.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.800
OK.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.650
Now, as I said, all of
this stuff you can actually

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.960
do today with our product.

